What it removes: the single store acquisition in epic_hosted_seat_occupancies,
restoring the split boundary after the history/current read.

--- first attempt: INCONCLUSIVE, not a kill ---
Hung ~48 minutes with the test binary at 0% CPU and no verdict; terminated.
Cause was the harness, not the production change: barrier_case asserted
inside std::thread::scope before calling barrier.release(), so the scope
waited forever to join a reader nobody would wake. Full process evidence is
retained in M-COH-first-attempt-INCONCLUSIVE.txt.

--- harness fix ---
The scope now only observes; barrier.release() runs on every path; verdicts
are reached after both joins; the observation loop is bounded; and every run
is wall-clock bounded so a coordination defect reports a timeout instead of
hanging.

